The image is the inside front cover of a vintage pulp-style magazine titled:

EGO HYGIENE
Edition 1: Orientation

The page features aged parchment texture, darkened worn edges, subtle foxing marks, faint concentric circles in the center, and small crystal formations in the lower corners.

Centered text reads:

Orientation establishes your point of reference.
You can enter from anywhere.

The animation should simulate subtle post-processing effects only, as if the physical paper is gently alive.

Allowed motion:

– Extremely faint floating dust particles drifting slowly across frame
– Very subtle warm light shimmer near the bottom center glow
– Soft grain fluctuation, like old film stock breathing
– Slight uneven flicker in the paper tone (very subtle)
– Minimal light pulse across the faint circular diagram (barely visible)

NOT allowed:

– No camera motion
– No object movement
– No text movement
– No crystal movement
– No wind
– No glow intensification beyond subtle shimmer
– No dramatic lighting changes
– No mystical effects
– No particles interacting with text

The effect should feel like:

A printed page resting in still air.
An artifact breathing quietly.
Calibration.
Stillness.
A held breath before descent.

Duration: 6–8 seconds.
Loopable.
Seamless beginning and ending.

Overall tone: restrained, analog, tactile, archival.
